# Generated meshes - every one is reproducible from the explorer or its python
# twin in seconds, and together they run to ~230 MB.
*.msh
*.vtu
*.stl
*_foam/
*.zip
*.skill

# solver runs: meshes, cases and data the app writes.  Everything in here is
# reproducible from the geometry parameters plus the settings.
runs/
*.cas.h5
*.dat.h5

# Generated reports.  Every one of these is rebuilt by a button in seconds -
# the stage-1 report from correlations.py alone, the others from results.json
# beside them - and committing build output means the first person to press
# that button has a dirty tree and a `git pull` that aborts.  Which is exactly
# what happened.  The DATA stays in git: study.json is the definition and
# results.json is the measurement.  The HTML is neither.
studies/*/report.html
studies/*/report_en.html
studies/*/overview.html

# the histories re-spelled as CSV.  Nothing in here that results.json does
# not already carry, and the button regenerates the lot in a second.
studies/*/history/

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# editors / os
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
